  "content": {
    "id": "p52-g92-95",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the value(s) of $k$ for the following to have no real roots.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p52-g92-95-a",
        "type": "question",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$kx^2+6x+3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k>3$.\n\nRequire $\\Delta=36-12k<0$.",
          "worked": "For $k\\ne0$, no real roots require $\\Delta<0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=6^2-4(k)(3)\\\\\\Delta&=36-12k\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}36-12k&<0\\\\k&>3\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt $k=0$, the equation is $6x+3=0$, which has a real root, so this case does not qualify.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p52-g92-95-b",
        "type": "question",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2+2x+k+3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k>-2$.\n\nRequire $\\Delta=-4k-8<0$.",
          "worked": "The leading coefficient is $1$, so no real roots require $\\Delta<0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=2^2-4(1)(k+3)\\\\\\Delta&=-4k-8\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}-4k-8&<0\\\\k&>-2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p52-g92-95-c",
        "type": "question",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(k-1)^2x^2-(2k-1)x+1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k<\\dfrac34$.\n\nUse $\\Delta=4k-3<0$. The degree-changing value $k=1$ does not qualify.",
          "worked": "For $k\\ne1$, no real roots require $\\Delta<0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=\\bigl(-(2k-1)\\bigr)^2-4(k-1)^2(1)\\\\\\Delta&=4k^2-4k+1-4k^2+8k-4\\\\\\Delta&=4k-3\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4k-3&<0\\\\k&<\\frac34\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt $k=1$, the equation is $-x+1=0$, which has a real root, so this case does not qualify.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p52-g92-95-d",
        "type": "question",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$kx^2+(2k+3)x+(k+1)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k<-\\dfrac98$.\n\nUse $\\Delta=8k+9<0$. The degree-changing value $k=0$ does not qualify.",
          "worked": "For $k\\ne0$, no real roots require $\\Delta<0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(2k+3)^2-4k(k+1)\\\\\\Delta&=4k^2+12k+9-4k^2-4k\\\\\\Delta&=8k+9\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}8k+9&<0\\\\k&<-\\frac98\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt $k=0$, the equation is $3x+1=0$, which has a real root, so this case does not qualify.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
